WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.500
OPENING

00:15.610 --> 00:18.140
if it moves, it will have to release heat energy.

00:18.350 --> 00:20.940
I'm certain that they're lurking around this area.

00:21.380 --> 00:22.220
Attention!

00:22.220 --> 00:25.190
We've detected the sound of water discharging from
torpedo tubes which we believe belong to the Ishin.

00:25.190 --> 00:26.150
What?!

00:42.270 --> 00:44.610
Section 5, all high altitude airships lost!

00:44.610 --> 00:46.700
Cannot download data!

00:47.940 --> 00:50.380
Have you located the Ishin using sonar?

00:50.380 --> 00:52.610
There's too much baffle and it's hard to pinpoint.

00:52.610 --> 00:56.050
I don't care! Estimate their possible range
of movement from the Ishin's speed!

00:56.050 --> 00:58.140
Execute ASROC saturation attack
in passive mode!

01:01.120 --> 01:03.090
Torpedoes, incoming!
There's over a hundred of 'em!

01:03.860 --> 01:05.490
They sure are scattering them everywhere!

01:05.490 --> 01:07.730
Activate Masker. Fire decoy!

01:07.730 --> 01:08.390
Aye, sir!

01:22.010 --> 01:24.880
W-What the?! What the heck's going on?

01:24.880 --> 01:27.220
It's okay, Sana. Don't worry.

01:27.220 --> 01:28.280
But...

01:28.280 --> 01:31.220
This ship's built strong enough
that a little shaking won't sink it.

01:31.220 --> 01:32.710
Right, Joe?

01:33.490 --> 01:36.620
Yeah. We should just leave
everything up to that guy.

01:38.960 --> 01:52.330
Sora ni toketa hane o matoi tobitate tsubasa de

01:38.960 --> 01:45.570
Cloaked in feathers melted into the sky

01:45.570 --> 01:52.340
Take flight on wings

02:06.680 --> 02:09.850
Morokute nigai kajitsu no you ni

02:06.690 --> 02:09.860
Like fragile but bitter fruit

02:09.850 --> 02:13.060
Hito no kokoro o miryou suru no

02:09.860 --> 02:13.070
It fascinates people's hearts

02:13.060 --> 02:16.160
Togi sumasareta shiroi yubi de

02:13.070 --> 02:14.570
The shadow that manipulates

02:14.570 --> 02:16.170
With sharpened fingers gleaming white

02:16.160 --> 02:19.330
Ayatsuru kage wa chi no kaori

02:16.170 --> 02:19.340
Smells of blood

02:19.330 --> 02:32.330
Shizumi aseta kodou o yobi samasu shi no sasayaki

02:19.340 --> 02:25.780
The whisper of Death

02:25.780 --> 02:32.340
That awakens fading heartbeats

02:33.310 --> 02:39.680
Sora ni toketa hane o matoi

02:33.320 --> 02:39.690
Cloaked in feathers melted into the sky

02:39.680 --> 02:45.920
Tobitatsu no wa gin no tsubasa

02:39.690 --> 02:45.930
Silver wings take flight

02:45.920 --> 02:52.400
Fukai kaze ni tsume o tatete

02:45.930 --> 02:52.400
Become the power that tears at deep winds

02:52.400 --> 03:02.130
Kirisaku chikara to nare

02:52.400 --> 03:02.140
With poised claws

03:03.120 --> 03:06.310
Brought to you by
BiG-GuY Fansubbing

03:07.020 --> 03:12.320
Episode 7
Scheme

03:08.180 --> 03:09.950
Did you hear the
submarine imploding?

03:09.950 --> 03:11.890
We cannot confirm
due to bubble noise.

03:12.320 --> 03:15.290
We have no choice but to wait
until these bubbles die down.

03:24.670 --> 03:27.470
Looks like we've been spotted
from the sky by a P-X.

03:27.470 --> 03:30.930
If they launch another saturation attack,
we've got no more decoys!

03:31.340 --> 03:34.380
We've destroyed the airships
covering this area, right?

03:34.380 --> 03:38.180
Yeah, now their ships can only navigate by sight.

03:38.510 --> 03:40.650
Good. Emergency surface!

03:40.650 --> 03:43.010
Let's show 'em how we pirates
can steer this vessel!

03:54.460 --> 03:56.020
Port, port!

04:02.270 --> 04:03.570
What's going on?

04:03.570 --> 04:05.940
Escort vessel Okuno has collided
with the right helm of this ship!

04:05.940 --> 04:07.530
Bulkheads, locking down!

04:12.880 --> 04:14.850
Detecting powerful jamming signal!

04:14.850 --> 04:17.550
Unable to use electronic guidance!
Switch to laser guidance!

04:17.550 --> 04:18.580
Roger!

04:21.860 --> 04:23.290
Missiles approaching!

04:23.290 --> 04:25.120
Launch interceptor missiles!

04:42.980 --> 04:45.240
It's locked on to me! I'm ejecting!

04:48.480 --> 04:50.120
The air unit has been completely wiped out.

04:50.120 --> 04:52.190
What the hell are the escort vessels doing?

04:52.190 --> 04:56.250
Without any reports from the airships, there's
a danger of friendly fire, so they can't risk shooting.

05:23.150 --> 05:24.620
How could this have happened?

05:24.620 --> 05:26.490
The electronic encircling net
ended up ruining us!

05:26.490 --> 05:29.320
Commander, we're receiving a shortwave
transmission from the chief of Satsuma.

05:29.320 --> 05:30.760
Put him through!

05:31.660 --> 05:34.630
This is Buichi Nakahira, the chief of Satsuma.

05:34.630 --> 05:39.400
Our marine rescue vessel is training
10 km south of you.

05:39.400 --> 05:42.230
We'll send help over right away. Over and out.

05:42.800 --> 05:46.210
Training? Those damn Satsuma tanuki...

05:47.840 --> 05:49.900
We've just entered Satsuma territorial waters.

05:51.650 --> 05:54.340
We will now enter the secret underground dock.

05:54.720 --> 05:56.180
It's a tight fit, so be careful.

05:56.180 --> 05:57.280
Aye-aye, sir.

06:33.520 --> 06:35.180
Wow!

06:35.860 --> 06:36.820
Huh?

06:36.820 --> 06:39.490
You gave 'em quite a show, Toraji!

06:39.490 --> 06:43.690
Thanks to you, the National Defense Force
owes us one!

06:45.870 --> 06:47.940
Who the heck is this old guy?

06:47.940 --> 06:51.970
He's the chief of Satsuma territory
and will be harboring you.

06:51.970 --> 06:54.510
Then you must be Buichi Nakahira.

06:54.510 --> 06:59.250
Yes. And are you Councilor Tsurusawa's son?

06:59.250 --> 07:02.550
I'm Jin Tsurusawa. Nice to meet you.

07:02.550 --> 07:07.660
Leave everything to me.
Toraji's told me all about you guys.

07:07.660 --> 07:09.820
Take them to the mansion.

07:09.820 --> 07:12.030
Yes, sir.

07:12.030 --> 07:13.930
This way, please.

07:18.130 --> 07:21.200
Hey, hold on. Where do you think you're going?

07:21.200 --> 07:25.240
I was going to rest my weary body at your mansion.

07:25.240 --> 07:27.540
I told you to wait!

07:27.540 --> 07:30.840
There's a lot I want to tell you.

07:31.280 --> 07:33.140
Here we go again...

07:42.520 --> 07:43.930
Hey, hey...

07:43.930 --> 07:47.530
It's almost like the wall's come down
and Logos and Revinus have become one!

07:47.530 --> 07:50.800
Since the old times, Satsuma has always been
a country that values justice.

07:50.800 --> 07:56.000
By doing away with discrimination against the people
of Revinus who fought with us in the AU battle,

07:56.000 --> 07:58.940
we are trying to unite as the country of Satsuma.

08:07.150 --> 08:08.980
Whoa! Awesome!

08:11.220 --> 08:13.310
Shiba's not with them.

08:15.560 --> 08:17.460
This is Bravo 6.

08:17.460 --> 08:19.390
This is Romeo 101.

08:19.390 --> 08:21.130
Were you able to get the pictures
to use as evidence?

08:21.130 --> 08:23.930
No problem. There haven't been any mistakes.

08:24.300 --> 08:28.670
I just transmitted them to headquarters under
the National Defense Force's agent code.

08:28.800 --> 08:31.410
Our target is in Nakahira's mansion.

08:31.410 --> 08:33.040
I'll send you the location data,

08:33.040 --> 08:34.910
so leave Kyoushiro there and meet up with them.

08:34.910 --> 08:36.170
Roger.

08:36.580 --> 08:38.240
I'll leave the rest up to you.

08:38.710 --> 08:40.150
Where are you off to?

08:40.150 --> 08:43.780
I'm off to shoot... The second shot...

08:45.350 --> 08:47.180
I won't miss, this time.

08:50.060 --> 08:52.090
It's huge!

08:52.090 --> 08:54.630
The yard and the mansion are both humongous!

08:54.630 --> 08:55.600
Amazing!

08:57.200 --> 08:58.760
Welcome.

09:00.270 --> 09:01.770
Pathetic...

09:01.770 --> 09:03.740
These are the mansion's maids.

09:03.740 --> 09:07.240
If there is anything they can help you with,
please let them know.

09:07.240 --> 09:08.940
Anything?

09:08.940 --> 09:11.580
Hey, hey, I'm starving!

09:11.580 --> 09:14.220
A meal has already been prepared.

09:14.220 --> 09:15.620
Wow, really?

09:15.620 --> 09:17.020
But, before that...

09:17.020 --> 09:21.490
BATH

09:17.850 --> 09:22.720
Cut it out! I hate baths! Stop it!

09:26.290 --> 09:29.500
How dare they wash off all that dirt and grime
I've been saving...

09:29.500 --> 09:31.730
What if I catch a cold now?!

09:34.500 --> 09:37.400
Joe! Food! Food! Let's go get us some food!

09:40.680 --> 09:42.200
That's some scar you've got there.

09:43.280 --> 09:45.650
I'm sure you know what I want to talk to you about.

09:45.650 --> 09:50.690
I want you to join me in raising a flag of revolt
against Central Logos.

09:50.690 --> 09:52.720
I'm just a plain ol' pirate.

09:52.720 --> 09:54.920
I have no intention of raising a flag
or a banner for that matter.

09:56.160 --> 09:58.060
No, that won't do!

09:58.060 --> 10:01.760
Did you see the submarine fleet
in the underground dock?

10:01.760 --> 10:04.420
That's Satsuma's trump card.

10:06.370 --> 10:09.600
But unfortunately, we don't have anyone
who can operate them.

10:09.940 --> 10:13.170
We need a man like you.

10:13.170 --> 10:18.510
Sorry Buichi, but jobs like conquering the world
really don't suit me.

10:18.980 --> 10:21.020
Ask someone else, okay?

10:21.020 --> 10:23.820
Then why did you go up against
the National Defense Force?

10:23.820 --> 10:26.450
Old man Chikura asked me to before he died.

10:26.950 --> 10:29.550
He asked me to protect that girl.

10:30.160 --> 10:31.960
That's all I have to say.

10:31.960 --> 10:33.860
We'll be staying with you a while.

10:33.860 --> 10:35.360
Wait, Toraji.

10:35.360 --> 10:38.590
That wasn't the only thing Chikura said
before he died, is it?

10:38.930 --> 10:43.570
Carry out... your mission!

10:43.570 --> 10:46.600
You must do what you were meant to do.

10:47.070 --> 10:49.310
He must've said something to you.

10:49.310 --> 10:51.680
It's time you start conducting yourself
in a proper manner!

10:55.780 --> 10:58.310
All right, I understand.

10:59.190 --> 11:01.460
I won't bother you anymore.

11:01.460 --> 11:03.820
Hope you have a relaxing time here.

11:04.590 --> 11:06.790
I was planning to do just that.

11:12.000 --> 11:15.770
That idiot. How long is he going to
live aimlessly like that?

11:19.210 --> 11:20.670
It's this way.

11:24.080 --> 11:27.180
We haven't maintained it for some time though.

11:27.180 --> 11:31.240
That's okay. I just felt like playing a little.

11:31.620 --> 11:36.080
I see. If there is anything else you need,
please let me know.

11:40.700 --> 11:42.960
Do you remember that sound from the other day?

11:42.960 --> 11:44.100
Yes.

11:44.100 --> 11:47.360
It was out of tune, right?
I want to recreate that sound.

11:55.810 --> 11:59.780
These are the infiltration photos
sent under the agent code.

11:59.780 --> 12:02.750
Have you been able to get in touch
with that agent?

12:02.750 --> 12:07.660
He used an emergency line,
so we are not able to contact him.

12:07.660 --> 12:09.060
That's okay.

12:09.060 --> 12:12.150
The fact still remains that
this is indisputable evidence.

12:13.130 --> 12:16.130
So Shiba and Nakahira
have joined forces, have they?

12:16.130 --> 12:18.330
That could be a problem.

12:18.330 --> 12:20.800
The Ishin together with that submarine fleet.

12:20.800 --> 12:23.370
And if Shiba takes command of it all...

12:23.370 --> 12:26.170
Let's dispatch the
National Defense Force's main fleet.

12:26.170 --> 12:27.580
So you're going to start a war?

12:27.580 --> 12:32.910
We're just going to threaten Nakahira
to make him hand over Shiba and the Ishin.

12:32.910 --> 12:35.320
Will he hand them over without a fight?

12:35.320 --> 12:38.990
I doubt they're in a position to stand up against us.

12:38.990 --> 12:44.050
So he may be a sworn friend,
but "necessity knows no law." Right?

12:44.530 --> 12:48.990
If he whines about it, then we'll just shoot
a Harpoon right into their faces.

13:01.880 --> 13:03.440
Did it sound like this?

13:03.440 --> 13:06.210
Yeah, something like that.

13:06.210 --> 13:09.610
I want to play that piece we played before again.

13:17.530 --> 13:20.460
Please, Sana. I beg of you.

13:21.360 --> 13:22.290
Jin...

13:22.730 --> 13:24.790
Please... just one more time.

13:27.070 --> 13:30.300
All right. I'll try.

13:54.660 --> 13:56.860
Isn't the ocean just wonderful?

13:57.900 --> 13:59.660
Don't you think so, Oryo?

14:15.750 --> 14:18.450
Sana! Are you okay, Sana?

14:19.220 --> 14:21.820
One more time. Just one more time...

14:21.820 --> 14:23.310
Please play it again!

14:25.260 --> 14:27.160
All right.

14:30.030 --> 14:32.090
Hang in there, Sana!

14:32.600 --> 14:34.500
Come on, you can do it!

14:34.500 --> 14:35.470
Okay.

14:43.810 --> 14:44.870
Jin.

14:45.280 --> 14:47.080
I think you should stop now.

14:50.720 --> 14:51.390
Jin!

14:51.390 --> 14:52.750
Shut up!

15:09.670 --> 15:10.970
Sana!

15:14.280 --> 15:18.780
The night view we saw together from here
was the best, wasn't it?

15:18.780 --> 15:22.680
Yes, we had fun back then.

15:23.080 --> 15:25.790
But before I knew it,

15:25.790 --> 15:28.320
you were looking at a different view.

15:28.320 --> 15:30.260
By yourself.

15:31.630 --> 15:33.360
So which one is it?

15:33.360 --> 15:37.820
Are you here for revenge or
are you just following orders?

15:43.400 --> 15:47.170
Go ahead and shoot me.
If you're here for revenge...

15:51.210 --> 15:54.700
But if that's not the case, then...

16:05.530 --> 16:07.630
The National Defense Force's main fleet
has launched an attack on us.

16:07.630 --> 16:08.990
Are you serious?

16:10.030 --> 16:11.620
See you later, Oryo.

16:23.040 --> 16:25.200
This is Bravo 6.

16:27.680 --> 16:30.310
I see. Continue your surveillance.

16:40.530 --> 16:42.500
Her fever isn't going down.

16:42.500 --> 16:45.330
Both her pulse and heart rate
are at a dangerous level.

16:45.330 --> 16:48.100
S-She 's not going to die, is she?

16:48.100 --> 16:50.100
Hey, Princess, hang in there!

16:50.100 --> 16:53.210
She should be taken to a specialist right away.

16:53.210 --> 16:56.540
Let's do that. There's not a minute to waste.

16:56.540 --> 16:59.070
Understood. Please take her.

17:00.750 --> 17:04.080
This is Delta 2. The target is on the move.

17:04.080 --> 17:06.520
Roger. We'll follow her from the air.

17:06.520 --> 17:07.520
Let's go.

17:07.520 --> 17:08.610
Yes, ma'am.

17:21.670 --> 17:23.670
Damn Satsuma tanuki.

17:23.670 --> 17:26.400
I'm gonna expose your true colors. You just wait...

17:48.300 --> 17:49.500
What is it?

17:49.500 --> 17:52.900
The chief of Satsuma territory
is calling on the hot line.

17:52.900 --> 17:54.270
All right.

17:57.270 --> 18:00.440
Well, if it isn't Nakahira. It's been a while.

18:00.440 --> 18:05.000
Mr. Katsura, what on Earth is going on here?
I'd like an explanation.

18:05.380 --> 18:09.980
We've gotten a report that you're harboring
the leader of the pirates

18:09.980 --> 18:14.440
and rising in revolt against us Central Logos.

18:14.760 --> 18:17.790
All I did was send a fleet out to keep it in check.

18:17.790 --> 18:19.760
Who fed you this nonsense?

18:19.760 --> 18:22.250
It's not nonsense. Look at this.

18:25.330 --> 18:27.360
There you have it.

18:27.670 --> 18:32.830
But depending on what you do,
this whole crisis can be averted.

18:33.710 --> 18:35.810
What do you mean?

18:35.810 --> 18:40.640
Hand the Ishin and Shiba over to the
National Defense Force.

18:41.250 --> 18:47.020
If you comply, we'll withdraw our fleet and
disregard our suspicions of Satsuma's rebellion.

18:47.860 --> 18:51.160
I'll give you 24 hours.

18:51.160 --> 18:55.150
I trust you will make the right decision.

18:56.660 --> 18:59.100
What are you gonna do, Buichi?

19:00.700 --> 19:03.870
Hand us over and close the deal
with Central Logos?

19:03.870 --> 19:05.540
Idiot!

19:05.540 --> 19:07.070
No matter what I do,

19:07.070 --> 19:10.340
I'm sure the National Defense Force will station itself
here on the pretense of maintaining public order.

19:10.610 --> 19:13.650
To think I allowed a spy in here...

19:13.650 --> 19:17.420
It may have been a spy, but not from
the National Defense Force.

19:17.420 --> 19:19.010
If not, then who?

19:19.620 --> 19:21.490
Y-You don't think...

19:23.390 --> 19:25.380
It's showtime!

19:28.000 --> 19:29.200
What was that?!

19:29.200 --> 19:31.030
Escort vessel "Kuragari" struck!

19:31.030 --> 19:33.560
It is believed to be a torpedo attack
from the Satsuma fleet!

19:33.830 --> 19:36.140
How dare they? They're just Logos outsiders!

19:36.140 --> 19:37.760
Never mind! Fire back!

19:42.410 --> 19:44.240
N-No way! Counter-attack!

19:53.590 --> 19:55.490
Attention all citizens.

19:56.090 --> 20:01.190
The National Defense Force is currently in battle
with ourSatsuma Self-Defense Force.

20:01.800 --> 20:05.430
Please move away from the coastline
and evacuate to higher ground.

20:01.830 --> 20:02.830
Joe!

20:02.830 --> 20:03.900
We gotta run!

20:03.900 --> 20:05.970
Jin...

20:05.430 --> 20:13.140
Only emergency vehicles wil be allowed on the road.
All others, please walk to your destinations.

20:05.970 --> 20:08.740
Where are you? Jin?

20:08.740 --> 20:13.440
If it's for you, Jin... I'll try my best...

20:13.440 --> 20:14.670
I repeat...

20:15.740 --> 20:19.150
Who was it?! Who gave the order to attack?!

20:19.150 --> 20:22.520
Satsuma struck first:
We had no choice but to counterattack!

20:22.520 --> 20:24.850
Satsuma struck first?

20:24.850 --> 20:28.060
Chief of Staff, about the agent
who sent that picture...

20:28.060 --> 20:30.660
Back off! This isn't the time for that!

20:30.660 --> 20:32.390
No, please listen!

20:32.390 --> 20:36.900
I checked the agent code
and found that it's a lost number!

20:36.900 --> 20:38.520
Lost number?

20:41.030 --> 20:45.840
It looks like we've been manipulated
by Drake all along.

20:51.180 --> 20:52.280
There it is!

20:52.280 --> 20:54.540
We're almost there, Sana! Hang in there!

21:24.980 --> 21:26.580
My firepower's in a different league.

21:26.580 --> 21:28.340
Come out before you get hurt.

21:29.050 --> 21:30.020
Qing Lang!

21:30.620 --> 21:31.580
Damn!

21:37.420 --> 21:38.580
Damn it.

21:45.170 --> 21:46.500
I see.

21:46.500 --> 21:48.160
Good job. Thanks.

21:52.940 --> 21:55.640
So, what will you do now, Jin Tsurusawa?

21:56.940 --> 21:59.540
I'm going to give you a warm welcome.

22:25.210 --> 22:29.720
Nagai kioku no hate ni

22:25.210 --> 22:29.680
If at the end of our long memory

22:29.680 --> 22:35.520
Time will tear us apart

22:29.720 --> 22:35.550
Toki ga bokura o wakatsu nara

22:37.560 --> 22:44.200
If at the end of my sweet memory with you

22:37.590 --> 22:44.230
Kimi to amai kioku no hate ni

22:44.200 --> 22:50.500
You and I become one again

22:44.230 --> 22:50.540
Mata bokura hitotsu nara

22:50.500 --> 22:57.680
From a quietly stretched arm's length away

22:50.540 --> 22:57.710
Sotto te nobashita kyori kara

22:57.680 --> 23:02.380
I will search for the meaning

22:57.710 --> 23:02.420
lmi o sagasu kara

23:02.380 --> 23:08.220
Can you hear it? The words dance in midair

23:02.420 --> 23:08.260
Kikoeru? Kotoba ga chuu ni mau

23:08.220 --> 23:14.030
We shall meet when our wish is granted

23:08.260 --> 23:14.060
Kanaeta toki ni deau

23:14.030 --> 23:17.700
Leaving only their reverse behind

23:14.060 --> 23:17.730
Reverse dake nokoshite

23:17.700 --> 23:21.100
The torn words

23:17.730 --> 23:21.130
Chigireta kotoba

23:21.100 --> 23:27.230
Blurred time and light

23:21.130 --> 23:27.270
Kasureta jikan to hikari

23:29.410 --> 23:33.740
I have found them now

23:29.440 --> 23:33.780
lma, mitsuketa kara

23:35.680 --> 23:47.150
Next Episode

23:44.520 --> 23:47.150
Next time on Innocent Venus:

23:47.660 --> 23:49.560
<b><i>Episode</i></b> 8
<b><i>Loss</i></b>

23:47.890 --> 23:49.160
"Loss"
